{"In handleCancelBooking.ts, handleNewBooking.ts, and bookings.tsx, deleteScheduledEmailReminder and deleteScheduledSMSReminder are called inside .forEach without await, so their returned promises are never awaited. Errors are silently discarded and callers proceed as if cancellation succeeded, meaning reminders for cancelled or rescheduled bookings may still fire.": 0.9316626191139221, "When immediateDelete is true in emailReminderManager.ts, the function POSTs to SendGrid to cancel the email and then immediately returns without deleting the WorkflowReminder row from the database, leaving orphaned records that persist until the scheduled date passes.": 0.9206538796424866, "The CRON handler first deletes ALL email workflowReminder rows whose scheduledDate <= now with no filter on cancelled, running before the cancellation block. If a reminder was marked cancelled=true but its scheduledDate is in the past, the row is deleted from the DB without ever sending the cancel request to SendGrid.": 0.642768919467926, "The scheduleSMSReminders CRON has no cancellation block for cancelled=true reminders. It only has deleteMany cleanup which deletes ALL SMS reminders where scheduledDate <= now(), including those with cancelled=true, creating architectural inconsistency with scheduleEmailReminders CRON.": 0.6918882131576538}